(Others make various sounds)

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:54.320
MARK: Anyway. Just vlogging. Don't mind me. Cas' (as in "casual") vlog.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.640
Someone off camera: Heh, "cas' vlog" (laughs)
MARK: How's it goin'?

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.600
(Mark and AJ laugh. AJ says something but it's indistinguishable because Mark is laughing over him)

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.500
MARK: Everyone's just a lumbering beast as they go around.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.660
(Someone talks off camera; indistinguishable)
MARK (to Nate): Hey. How's that cas' banana?

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:06.960
NATE: Oh this c- it's super cas', man.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.780
MARK: Tha- That's a cas'-
NATE: Nothin'- nothin' to write home about but- so banana.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.880
MARK: You look very cas', I mean, I'll be honest.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.160
MARK(to Peter): Ooh, nice cas' soda. (Someone begins talking in the background)
Peter: Thank you.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.140
MARK: Yeah. Oh, that's a cool cas' shirt.
PETER: Right, right?
MARK: Yeah. Very cas'.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:20.600
MARK: Some cas' singing going on there.
David: Rock the cas'-bah.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.220
MARK: SHUT THE FU-

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:28.260
(laughter off camera)
(Mark starts smacking his lips)
(People talking off camera)

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:32.860
PETER: Alright, this is good. Uh, oh wait a minute, actually- hmm.. eh...

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.560
(Someone off camera says something in a Russian accent)

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.360
(Nate makes a low sound while using the fire extinguisher)

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.880
AJ: Very professional stance there.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.880
NATE: *Makes another low sound*

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.440
NATE: "This is really not as fun as it looks..."

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.460
Background Voice #1: "Yeah..."
Background Voice #2: *chuckles* "It looks pretty fun!"

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.800
Background #3: "Did Nate finish early?"
"Yeah."

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:54.860
*Snickering in the background*

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:56.720
Background #3: "I knew he'd finish early".

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:00.960
(Mark's making fart noises whenever he "squishes" MatPat's head)

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.980
Man in background: *yelling* Leave them alone this is MY resturant!

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.460
Man in background: Oh sh***t. PEEEEEN

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.660
*Laughing ensues*

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:12.780
(farting noise from mark)

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:13.800
(slithering pbht noise from mark)

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.880
MatPat: I don't know about you, but when I'm filming YouTube Videos at two o'clock in the morning

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.900
About killing animatronic robots,

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.060
I drink

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.080
~Diet Coke~

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.520
Please give us money.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:29.520
*a lot of different laughs mixed with "please"*

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.640
Look- Look at this. Look at it.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.720
*thousand yard stare* Please.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.360
*everyone erupts in laughter*

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.360
This is for you fan girls out there!

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:46.640
*A very extended low groan*

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:47.720
*very quiet* Okay

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:48.680
I'm ashamed.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:50.600
*someone out of shot* Mark you over shot!

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:51.440
Oh, Alex!

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.440
*whole room laughing*

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.300
MARK: Good job! *thumbs up*

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.600
MARK: Hi! So, yeah, it's been, uh, really busy this week

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:04.600
What you just saw, was us filming, uh, for the 5 Nights at Freddy's musical

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.980
with Random Encounters and NateWantsToBattle and also,

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:09.200
MatPat from The Game Theorists, you saw him there.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.680
This is not sponsored by Diet Coke, they would never sponsor us.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:15.000
So, we've been incredibly busy with that.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.740
If you remember last week, I put out a video called "Markiplier Catches a Pen in his Mouth",

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:22.000
which is the (*thumbs up*) epitome of entertainment that we have on this channel.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.900
That's a whole 'nother story, but that was filmed, uh, in the first session that we were doing

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:30.600
for the Five Night's at Freddy's musical with those guys, that was at NateWantsToBattle's place.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.180
He's a really cool guy! Thank you so much for letting me use your bed...

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:38.160
...that sounds weird, but you'll see what it means in the video when it finally comes out!

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.360
So, uh, that, compounded with the Warcraft IRL ((video is called "ALL OUT WAR!!"))

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.280
uh, capture the flag thing we were doing with, like, 30 OTHER YOUTUBERS!

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:50.100
It was a HUGE bash! I mean, I mentioned it in a video that I was doing before, but...

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:54.820
It's just nuts! The amount of stuff that has been crammed into this week.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:58.100
And, uh, that doesn't even count the work that we've been doing on the show

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:01.760
uh, Matt, Ryan and I, I've mentioned this before, but we're working on a show

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:05.920
and the script is basically done, we've just been doing final reviews

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:11.000
before we submit it. And, ALSO, I've been working on a project with Jack and Danny

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:16.420
And we've just been starting on that, and that's an even BIGGER project, than the one I'm working on with Matt and Ryan

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:19.160
So, it's all kind of culminated on this WEEK

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:23.440
And, the most amazing thing, is that throughout all this craziness

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.460
And, all of the late nights, and all of the EXTREME amounts of coffee..

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:31.400
...almost lethal doses of caffeine that I've been imbibing,

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.420
uh, I've been having...FUN

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:38.960
Like, an UNBELIEVABLE amount of fun, like an incredible amount of motivating FUN!

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:42.880
It's the time of my life because, I've always said this to you guys

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:48.180
and I've always encouraged you guys to try to find this "fire" that motivates you to move forward.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.720
It's this fire that burns in your heart, and it burns so bright

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:57.560
that you wanna wake up, and immediately start working on it, and then you don't wanna fall asleep

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.340
because you still have more work to do.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:05.480
Like, that motivating fire is burning again in my heart, and that's amazing!

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:06.960
Like, it's so cool...

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:09.480
GOD, THAT CLICHE! I need to stop saying that...

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:16.720
...but it's COOL, in that it motivates me to move forward, and it motivates me to be more "creative"--quote, un-quote

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:19.980
"catch-a-pen-in-my-mouth" creative. Like, let's ignore that, but...

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:28.760
Uh, it's like, it motivates me to move forward and work on these big projects and it makes me so excited, to be able to do these things for you guys.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.500
And to be able to these things PERIOD, BECAUSE of you guys.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:38.000
So, that's why I actively encourage you guys to pursue, your creative side so much.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:41.900
Because, there's so much untapped potential, that you have yet to see

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:49.000
you're chipping away, at the artist inside of you, and you just need to keep digging, until you see the whole picture

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.000
of what you can do

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:58.000
And I'm trying to be, like, y'know, less than inspirational here, but, what- what I- what I'm just trying to get across to you guys,

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.300
is, there is potential, in ALL of us.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:06.000
And I've said it many times before, but know, that I do believe,

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:10.000
that in every single one of you,  there is a creative person.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:16.000
Or a non-creative person, or a very logical person, depending on how you are and how you look at the universe.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:22.000
But there's that person inside of you, that you can craft into the person that you want to become.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:27.800
And, no one is going to hand it to you, no one is going to give it to you, you have to work at that yourself

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:35.000
whether it's an artist under there or, uh, an engineer under there, or an inventor under there, or whatever is under there,

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.500
you craft that, into the person that you want to be.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:44.000
And it's these moments, when you have this fire burning in you and you have the inspiration driving you,

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.500
that make you, into that person, quicker!

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:54.500
I know that I tend to get overly excited about these things, but that's just because, I-I'm very passionate about this idea.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:07:03.700
That-the idea that that you guys have so much potential in you because, i-i-in me, like I know for a fact that I'm not incredibly talented.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:08.200
The only thing that I do, is ramble like an idiot, in front of a camera.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:12.100
But I get so much joy out of this gift that you guys have given me.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:24.000
Like the gift of this YouTube channel, like the gift of, the opportunity to be an idiot in front of a camera, the opportunity to, to do these amathing--amazing things with amazing people

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.500
I just want to get the words out! AAAHHHA

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:36.200
JUST KNOW, that in each, and every one of you, I firmly believe that there is the potential, to do something amazing.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:43.000
And it just takes time, to find that burning drive that moves you forward.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:48.200
SO I THINK THAT SUMMARIZES EVERYTHING, I'm not 100% sure but, I'm pretty sure that's everything that I wanted to say.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:51.000
So thank you everybody SO MUCH for watching.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:58.100
I will let you know, when these projects FINALLY come out, IN TIME, it's very close.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:06.000
I keep tantalizingly teasing it, but it is close, and it is amazing, and I am so grateful for the opportunity to be able to do it.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:16.000
So thank you everybody for watching, and as always, I WILL SEE YOU, in the next video, BUH-BYE!!!

